<div class="gl-tools-header">
	<h1>GL Maintenance</h1>
	<p class="hint">
		For a new migration, use <a href="/wizard">Step 5 of the Migration Wizard</a>, which runs these same actions in order.
		Use this page to run them again on a database that has already been migrated, for example after correcting
		<code>accounts</code> by hand or for a migration finished in an earlier session.
	</p>
</div>

<div class="gl-tools-grid">
	<section class="card gl-tool">
		<h3><span class="gl-tool-num" aria-hidden="true">1</span> Rebuild GL Accounts</h3>
		<p class="hint">
			Truncates and recreates <code>gl_accounts</code> from the staging <code>accounts</code> table, then runs the
			GL checks.
		</p>
		<label class="inline-label gl-tool-option">
			<input id="gl-wipe-journals" type="checkbox" />
			<span>Also truncate <code>gl_journal_headers</code> and <code>gl_journal_lines</code></span>
		</label>
		<div class="gl-tool-actions">
			<button id="btn-rebuild-gl-page" class="btn secondary" type="button">Rebuild GL Accounts</button>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="card gl-tool">
		<h3><span class="gl-tool-num" aria-hidden="true">2</span> Convert Account Numbers</h3>
		<p class="hint">
			Converts legacy Firebird account numbers to the new 4-digit GL numbers in every transactional table
			(<code>acc</code>, <code>accnr</code>, <code>accasset</code>, <code>siid</code>). Needs
			<code>gl_accounts</code> from step 1.
		</p>
		<p class="gl-tool-note">
			Safe to run more than once.
		</p>
		<div class="gl-tool-actions">
			<button id="btn-convert-transactional-accnr" class="btn secondary" type="button">Convert Account Numbers</button>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="card gl-tool">
		<h3><span class="gl-tool-num" aria-hidden="true">3</span> Validate GL</h3>
		<p class="hint">
			Read-only. Checks account types and postings, then the GAAP checks: trial balance, balance sheet identity,
			income statement accounts and cost of sales.
		</p>
		<p class="gl-tool-note">
			Run it after the <a href="/tools/gl-backfill">GL Backfill</a>, so the checks cover the posted journals.
		</p>
		<div class="gl-tool-actions">
			<button id="btn-gl-validate" class="btn secondary" type="button">Run GL Checks</button>
		</div>
	</section>
</div>

<section class="card gl-tools-result">
	<h3>Result</h3>
	<pre id="gl-tools-result" aria-live="polite">No action run yet.</pre>
</section>

<script src="/public/js/tools/gl-tools.js"></script>
